          "item": {
            "@type": "NewsArticle",
            "headline": "Tamil Nadu Police Used IT Rules to Ask X to Block 18 URLs Belonging to Ruling Party's Critics",
            "articleSection": "Policy & Rights",
            "abstract": "Tamil Nadu Police invoked Section 79(3)(b) of India's IT Act to request that X (formerly Twitter) block 18 URLs, which allegedly belong to DMK supporters who shared commentary criticising the Tamil Viduthalai Kazhagam party and the Chief Minister's office. The requests represent a pattern of state-level police agencies using federal IT law powers to suppress political speech online, bypassing judicial oversight. The incident adds to a growing record of India's content takedown infrastructure being used against domestic political dissent rather than solely for national security or harm-prevention purposes.",
            "url": "https://www.medianama.com/2026/05/223-tamil-nadu-police-x-block-18-urls-it-rules/",
            "publisher": {
              "@type": "NewsMediaOrganization",
              "name": "The AI Chronicle",
              "url": "https://theaichronicle.com",
              "logo": {
                "@type": "ImageObject",
